  clock: 4  # d377
  nonce: d377  # d377
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). CURRENT, worse than filed; the PRESCRIBED FIX conflicts with a standing rule.\n- Case-2a is still callee_symbol = local_symbols.get(attr_name) (py.py:8301-8303); the bare-name write symbol_by_name[item.name] = method_symbol is py.py:3342 (the item cites ~3525 and ~2453).\n- STRONGER REPRO: Order.finish calls self.save() and Order DEFINES save, yet it resolves to Fee.save (True, 0.85): last write wins, so a class's OWN method is replaced. Direct.go (no save of its own) also resolves self.save() to Fee.save.\n- FIX CORRECTION: resolving through caller_symbol.name.split('.')[0] is a name-based lookup, against the INV-mozas/INV-midag rule (an enclosing symbol is found by POSITION, never by name), and breaks for nested classes and same-named classes in one file. py.py already records method_to_enclosing_class_id[method_symbol.id] = symbol.id (WI-supat, ~3355); key Case-2a on that.\n- CROSS-ITEM: this bug is why INV-guviv's July stdlib-base gate is bypassed for same-file ancestors. A self.method() inherited call is resolved here before the linker's gated Site-1 runs. Fixing this makes the gate effective there.\n- PRIORITY: worth raising (two measurements show cost, and it defeats INV-guviv's gate). Proposal only; priority goes through the owner.\n- NOT CHECKED: the dst-blast-radius probe the item gates on; the pretix census discrepancy in the second discussion entry."  # d377
- op: discuss  # 4cd9
  at: '2026-10-03T17:37:53Z'  # 4cd9
  by: agent  # 4cd9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4cd9
  clock: 5  # 4cd9
  nonce: 4cd9  # 4cd9
  message: "IMPLEMENTED on local branch jgstern-agent/fix/kutal (base b7417402dc; not pushed, not merged): commits 2258c16112, 7419c6e16c, 6fc02d8d7f (62d650affd on the same branch is INV-guviv's Site-3 gate). Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/kutal.md.\n\nWHAT. py.py Case 2a no longer reads symbol_by_name. It reads FileAnalysis.methods_by_class_id: the def AND class statements of the OWN body of the class that `self` denotes, the later one in source order winning (runtime class-dict semantics). The class is found by POSITION, not name (_self_receiver_class_id): the innermost function frame binding `self`, if that frame is a non-@staticmethod method, via the WI-supat method_to_enclosing_class_id map. A closure reads its method's self; a module function, a staticmethod, or a nested def with its own self param denote no class -> unresolved (INV-fahub). The premise audit's prescribed fix (caller_symbol.name.split('.')[0]) was NOT used. A miss goes to the unresolved edge with the Site-1 hint, so same-file inherited methods are now resolved by the inherited_calls MRO walk (where INV-guviv's builtin-base gate is). Also: both Django ORM instance-write re-key sites share one refusal, _django_lineage_overrides (class or project base defines the method). Case 2a's bare-name bind had supplied that refusal for a same-file inherited override. The shared refusal also stops a pre-existing double count for a CROSS-file override (django: 18 user.save() sites with AbstractBaseUser.save in-tree).\n\nEVIDENCE. 15 new tests in test_py_self_method_class_scoped.py (11 red before the fix, for the expected reasons). One boundary test that pinned the old behaviour was updated (test_samefile_namesake_no_longer_shadows_case2a). Board smart-test, affected selection: 5791 passed, 2 xfailed, scoped coverage 100% on both changed sources, mypy ratchet clean. The item's named instances on pretix (3473fa7) were re-checked by call site:\n- ReauthView.post:170 now goes to ReauthView.get (was StopStaffSession.get, measurement 0016's FP).\n- CartPosition.update_listed_price_and_voucher:3277 now goes to CartPosition.save (was PrintLog.save). In this checkout CartPosition DOES define save at orders.py:3212, contrary to the 09-09 note.\n- Order.gracefully_delete:388 is now the django ORM delete (was PrintLog.delete).\n- CustomerSSOClient.check_client_secret's setter closure no longer binds Customer.save.\n\nCORPUS A/B by call site (each arm on its own pristine source snapshot and its own XDG cache):\n- django: 539 sites retargeted (536 from an unrelated class's method, to the caller's own method or a true ancestor's) and 138 wrong binds removed. COST: 2098 sites whose old same-file ANCESTOR target was right are now unresolved. Every one fails C3 because of a pre-existing inheritance cycle (unittest.TestCase bound to Django's own TestCase), filed as WI-ratid-mokat-fifon-hiros-nazun-bozim-mojak-jasin (P2). Also 24 sites lost where the class is assigned at runtime in setUp (self.CtxSyncHandler = CtxSyncHandler).\n- pretix: 349 retargeted from an unrelated class's method, 110 wrong binds removed. 102 sites read as lost are still resolved by the linker on another line of the same caller (filed: WI-sodor-muhif-bagit-vivos-kinap-nabig-gapim-hotav).\n- feast: 16 retargeted, all from an unrelated class's method.\nI read the random samples; every retarget I read was correct.\n\nNOT DONE / RESIDUALS:\n- The bare-name method write in symbol_by_name still exists. It still mis-binds bare calls such as open(...) -> ContentFile.open (django 56 sites, pretix 28): WI-barip-tidod-zivap-janan-jivaj-gohim-loriz-novol.\n- Methods under if/try in a class body are emitted as kind function: WI-modum-sanop-nohol-bihon-sikun-ritaj-fuzul-vilij.\n- Closures get no Site-1 hint and no oracle class: WI-mosof-zokuf-bafid-motir-mopaf-papaf-gozat-jilub.\n- The item asked for a directed dst-blast-radius probe before implementing; the call-site A/B above stands in its place."  # 4cd9
